  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "en-US",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmission00chal",
      "edition": "Memoirs of Missionary Priests, as well Secular as Regular, and of Other Catholics of both Sexes that have suffered Death in England on Religious Accounts, from the Year 1577 to 1684, a new edition revised and corrected by John Hungerford Pollen, S.J. (New York: P. J. Kenedy and Sons, 1924), Internet Archive full-text OCR.",
      "description": "Pollen's introduction, the two parts of the lives and the appendices; the contents and the index of names are dropped. The lives of one year form one chapter (the printed lives are not numbered). Pollen's bracketed additions and page notes are kept. Running heads and page numbers are dropped; the OCR was cleaned of line-break hyphens and the commonest recognition slips, and isolated slips remain. Raw OCR in sources/en-US-originals/.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Bp. Richard Challoner died in 1781 and the edition is of 1924, so the text is public domain."
    }
  ],
